<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Huai of Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 296 BCE</span> · Also known as Xiong Huai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Huai of Chu ruled the state of Chu from 328 to 299 BCE. Misled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> diplomat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-yi">Zhang Yi</a>, he broke his alliance with Qi and suffered heavy defeats by Qin. In 299 BCE he was lured to a meeting in Qin and held captive until his death in 296 BCE, an outrage long remembered in Chu and associated with the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qu-yuan">Qu Yuan</a>.</p></div>
